and to conserve a global environment which is fit to live in? In this book the author examines many of the major issues involved in these debates."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Vaclav Smil."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographies and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Power resources"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Food supply"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Environmental protection"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Conservation of Natural Resources"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Energy-Generating Resources"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Food Supply"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"TJ163.2 .S62 1987"},{"@edition":"19","@authority":"ddc","#text":"333.79"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0198285108 :"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0198285094"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^86028459^"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"14692465"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990006076360203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000123374118","#text":"Baker Library, Harvard Business School, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"TJ163.2 .S62 1987"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Baker Business"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990006076360203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"000607636"}},"processingDate":"2026-09-20T04:15Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"861022"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20020606"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990006076360203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.8 using\n\t\t\t\t\tMARC21slim_MODS3-8_XSL2-0.xsl (Revision 2.79 2025/03/28)"}},{"titleInfo":{"title":"Energy in nature and society","subTitle":"general energetics of complex systems"},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Smil, Vaclav.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"mau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"Massachusetts"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Cambridge, Mass"}}],"publisher":"The MIT Press","dateIssued":["c2008",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2008"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xi, 480 p. : ill., maps ; 23 cm."},"tableOfContents":["1. The universal link: energetics, energy, and power. Evolution of energetics: from Aristotle to Einstein ; Approaches to understanding: concepts, variables, units -- 2. Planetary energetics: hydrosphere, lithosphere. Sun: the star and its radiation ; Energy balance of the Earth: radiation fluxes ; Hydrosphere and atmosphere: thermal and mass fluxes ; Water and air in motion: kinetic fluxes ; Geoenergetics: heat, plate tectonics, volcanoes, earthquakes -- 3. Photosynthesis: bioenergetics of primary production. Photosynthetic pathways ; Global primary productivity ; Productivities of ecosystems and plants ; Phytomass stores ; Autotrophic scaling -- 4. Heterotrophic conversions: consumer bioenergetics. Metabolic capabilities ; Ectotherms and endotherms ; Locomotion ; Biomasses and productivities ; Heterotrophs in ecosystems -- 5. Human energetics: people as a simple heterotophs. Energy sources and basal metabolism ; Requirements and uncertainties ; Thermoregulation ; Limits of human performance ; Gathering, hunting and fishing -- Traditional food production: humans as a solar farmers. Extensive practices ; Permanent cropping ; Muscles, implements, machines ; Cropping intensification ; Traditional agricultures -- 7. Preindustrial complexification: prime movers and fuels in traditional societies. Animate power: human and animal muscles ; Water and wind: wheels and mills ; Phytomass fuels and metallurgy: wood, charcoal, crop residues ; Construction: methods and structures ; Transportation: roads and ships --","8. Fossil fuels: heat, light and prime movers. Coals: the earliest modern fuels ; Hydrocarbons: crude oils and natural gases ; From extraction to combustion: modern fossil-fuel industries ; Mechanical prime movers: engines and turbines ; Fossil-fueled electricity: generation and transmission -- 9. Fossil-fueled civilization: patterns and trends. Fuels ad fossil-fueled electricity : energy production and trade ; Nonfossil contributions: biomass and primary electricity ; Global consumption patterns: growth and inequality ; Qualitative changes: transitions and efficiencies ; Energy conservation: gains and rebounds -- 10. Energy costs: valuations and changes. Energy cost of energy: net gains ; Basic materials: from concrete to fertilizers ; Structures and products: from buildings to computers ; Crops and animal foods: subsidized diets ; Modern food system: gains, costs, efficiencies -- 11. Environmental consequences: metabolism of fossil-fueled civilization. Power densities: energy and land ; Energy conversions and heat rejection ; Energy and water ; Energy and the atmosphere ; Interference in grand biospheric cycles -- 12. Energetic correlates: complexities of high-energy civilization. Energy and the economy ; Energy and value ; Energy and the quality of life ; Energy and war ; Energy and the future -- 13. Grand patterns: energetic and other essentials. Energy in the biosphere ; Energy and the civilization ; The challenges ahead."],"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Vaclav Smil."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (p. [401]-459) and indexes."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Bioenergetics"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Energy budget (Geophysics)"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"QH510 .S63 2008"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"QT530"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"577/.13"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780262693561 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0262693569 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^2007002801"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"80359863"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990114439400203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000046073724X","#text":"Cabot Science Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"QH510 .S63 2008"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Cabot Science"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990114439400203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"011443940"}},"processingDate":"2024-04-07T05:15Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"070123"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20080428"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990114439400203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)"}},{"titleInfo":{"title":"Energy transitions","subTitle":"history, requirements, prospects"},"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Smil, Vaclav.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},"text"],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"cau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"California"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2010"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Santa Barbara, Calif. :"}},"publisher":"Praeger,","dateIssued":"c2010."},{"@eventType":"distribution","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York :"}},"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (US),","dateOther":{"@type":"distribution","#text":"2024."}}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marccategory","#text":"electronic resource"},{"@authority":"marcsmd","#text":"remote"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"","#text":"computer"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"","#text":"online resource"}],"extent":"1 online resource (190 p.)"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Energy transitions are fundamental processes behind the evolution of human societies: they both drive and are driven by technical, economic, and social changes. In a bold and provocative argument, Energy Transitions: History, Requirements, Prospects describes the history of modern society's dependence on fossil fuels and the prospects for the transition to a nonfossil world. Vaclav Smil, who has published more on various aspects of energy than any working scientist, makes it clear that this transition will not be accomplished easily, and that it cannot be accomplished within the timetables est"},"tableOfContents":"Energy systems : their basic properties -- Global transitions : universal patterns -- National transitions : commonalities and particularities -- Coming transitions : expectations and realities.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Vaclav Smil."},"Description based upon print version of record.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 157-166) and index."},{"@type":"language","#text":"English"}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Power resources"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Renewable energy sources"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"TJ808 .S64 2010"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"333.79"}],"relatedItem":[null,null,{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99153590071603941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9798400646133"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780313381782"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"031338178X"},{"@type":"doi","#text":"10.5040/9798400646133"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"2010002985"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"651599570"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"ocn505017554"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"505017554"}],"location":[null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/99153590071603941","processingDate":"2025-05-05T05:12Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"100205"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20101019"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"99153590071603941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)"}}]}}